      "gh:sections": [
        {
          "title": "Arc 0-1: Ghost Hacker Origin (The Phantom Purchase) - Structure Design",
          "content": "**Target Length:** 45 Pages\n**Format:** Wattpad / Vertical Scroll Manga Style\n**Theme:** Information Security, Social Engineering, Landauer's Principle (Information = Physics)"
        },
        {
          "title": "Character Roles",
          "content": "*   **Yuto:** The Victim. Relatable student, falls for a scam, isolated.\n*   **Ren:** The Protagonist. Lethargic hacker, wields NULL AXE.\n*   **Nei:** The Guide. Explains the theory (Landauer), operates the SIP Project Map.\n*   **Classmates:** The Society. Bystanders who turn into antagonists due to misunderstanding.\n\n---"
        },
        {
          "title": "Act 1: The Trap (Pages 1-8)",
          "content": "*Inciting Incident: Desire and the Click*\n\n*   **Page 1:** **[Scene: Classroom / Break time]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto looking at a group of popular students (mixed gender) chatting. Ren is sleeping at his desk in the background. Nei is reading a book quietly.\n    *   *Atmosphere:* Normal school life. Yuto feels slightly on the outside.\n*   **Page 2:** **[Scene: Classroom]**\n    *   *Visual:* Classmate A (Popular guy) shows off a \"Brand X\" limited edition item (sneakers or accessory).\n    *   *Dialogue:* \"Got the limited drop! Sold out in seconds.\"\n    *   *Action:* Friends admire it. Yuto thinks, \"I want that too...\"\n*   **Page 3:** **[Scene: Classroom -> Yuto's Room (Transition)]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto asking where he got it. Classmate A: \"You can't get it anymore. Resale is 3x the price.\"\n    *   *Beat:* Yuto's envy grows.\n*   **Page 4:** **[Scene: Yuto's Room / Night]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto lying in bed, smartphone light on his face. Scrolling SNS.\n    *   *Action:* \"Damn, it's so expensive...\" suddenly, an Ad appears. \"Emergency Stock! 80% OFF! Time Limited!\"\n*   **Page 5:** **[Scene: Yuto's Smartphone Screen]**\n    *   *Visual:* The fake site \"Wakuwaku Denki\" (or similar generic name). It looks legitimate *enough*.\n    *   *Detail:* Countdown timer: 05:00... 04:59...\n    *   *Monologue:* \"Is this real? But it's on a major SNS... must be safe.\"\n*   **Page 6:** **[Scene: Yuto's Room]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto hesitating, then running to get his parent's wallet (or his own card).\n    *   *Action:* Typing in details. Credit Card Number. Expiry.\n*   **Page 7:** **[Scene: Smartphone Input]**\n    *   *Visual:* The form asks for more than usual. \"ID for verification.\" \"Password (create a new one).\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto uses his standard password (the one he uses for everything). \"Just this once.\" *CLICK*.\n*   **Page 8:** **[Scene: Yuto's Room]**\n    *   *Visual:* \"Purchase Complete!\" \"We will ship tomorrow!\" 5-star reviews shown.\n    *   *Beat:* Yuto sighs in relief. \"I got it!\" He sleeps happily."
        },
        {
          "title": "Act 2: The Fall (Pages 9-20)",
          "content": "*Rising Action: The Scam Unfolds & Isolation*\n\n*   **Page 9:** **[Scene: Classroom / Next Day]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto smiling, looking at Classmate A.\n    *   *Monologue:* \"Just wait. I'll have one tomorrow.\" He almost speaks but decides to wait until he has it.\n*   **Page 10:** **[Scene: Yuto's Room / 3 Days Later]**\n    *   *Visual:* Checking the mailbox. Empty.\n    *   *Action:* Checking the tracking. \"Preparing for shipment.\"\n*   **Page 11:** **[Scene: Smartphone]**\n    *   *Visual:* Email from \"Support\". \"Shipping trouble. Please confirm your details via this link.\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto, anxious, clicks and enters info again. (Phishing Step 2).\n*   **Page 12:** **[Scene: Daily Life Montage]**\n    *   *Visual:* 2-3 days pass. Weird things happen. Spam emails increase. Strange phone calls (silent).\n    *   *Beat:* The creeping sense of wrongness.\n*   **Page 13:** **[Scene: Living Room]**\n    *   *Visual:* Mother/Father angry. \"The credit card was stopped! Someone tried to buy $5000 worth of gift cards!\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto turns pale. \"What?\"\n*   **Page 14:** **[Scene: Yuto's Room]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto rushes to the site.\n    *   *Result:* **404 Not Found.** The site is gone.\n*   **Page 15:** **[Scene: School / Morning]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto walks in. The atmosphere is heavy. Everyone looks at him.\n    *   *Action:* Classmate A approaches. \"Hey. What's with that message last night?\"\n*   **Page 16:** **[Scene: Classroom]**\n    *   *Visual:* Friend shows phone. Yuto's account sent: \"Click this link! It's awesome!\" and \"You're actually annoying lol.\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto: \"I didn't send this!\"\n*   **Page 17:** **[Scene: Classroom Chaos]**\n    *   *Visual:* Another girl screams. \"My private photos! Why are they on your timeline!?\"\n    *   *Explanation:* Yuto's account was hijacked and used to expose DM secrets.\n    *   *Dialogue:* \"You were the only one I told! Traitor!\"\n*   **Page 18:** **[Scene: Yuto's Panic]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto trying to login. \"Incorrect Password.\" \"Reset Password.\" -> \"Email not found.\"\n    *   *Beat:* Complete lockout.\n*   **Page 19:** **[Scene: Classroom Isolation]**\n    *   *Visual:* The class surrounds him. \"Die.\" \"Creep.\" \"Scammer.\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto curling up. The malice is palpable (visualized as dark static).\n*   **Page 20:** **[Scene: The Corner]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto alone at his desk, head down.\n    *   *Beat:* Total despair. \"It's all my fault...\""
        },
        {
          "title": "Act 3: Intervention & Visualization (Pages 21-30)",
          "content": "*The Turning Point: Enter the Ghost Hackers*\n\n*   **Page 21:** **[Scene: Classroom]**\n    *   *Visual:* The air is heavy/spiky. Nei walks over calmly.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"Are you okay?\"\n*   **Page 22:** **[Scene: Classroom]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto looks up, tears in eyes. Explains briefly. \"I didn't do it... but I did click...\"\n    *   *Action:* Nei listens, then turns. \"Ren. Ghost. What do we do?\"\n*   **Page 23:** **[Scene: Classroom]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren stretches, looking bored.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Ren: \"Ugh... what a pain. But... fine. Let's do it.\"\n*   **Page 24:** **[Scene: Countermeasure Montage (The Struggle)]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren/Nei instructing Yuto. \"Contact Support.\" \"Freeze accounts.\" \"Tell friends to ignore.\"\n    *   *Action:* Yuto trying to explain to friends.\n*   **Page 25:** **[Scene: Classroom / Reality Check]**\n    *   *Visual:* Friends shouting back. \"So what?! The photos are already out!\" \"You can't undo it!\"\n    *   *Beat:* Logic and security measures don't fix the *emotional* damage.\n*   **Page 26:** **[Scene: Yuto's Heartbreak]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto collapses internally. \"It's meaningless. I ruined everything.\"\n    *   *Dialogue:* Classmates: \"Just disappear.\"\n*   **Page 27:** **[Scene: Nei's Diagnosis]**\n    *   *Visual:* Nei looks at the air.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"Ren. It's Phantom Pain.\"\n    *   *Action:* Ren nods silently.\n*   **Page 28:** **[Scene: Device Activation]**\n    *   *Visual:* Nei pulls out a strange device (cube/sphere).\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"SIP Project Map: ON.\"\n*   **Page 29:** **[Scene: The Shift]**\n    *   *Visual:* A wave scans the room. The classroom texture changes. Wireframes overlay reality.\n    *   *Beat:* The \"Information Field\" is revealed.\n*   **Page 30:** **[Scene: Ghosts Appear]**\n    *   *Visual:* The \"static\" and \"malice\" take shape. Grotesque, glitchy ghosts clinging to the classmates and binding Yuto.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Classmates: \"What the?! VR?! Ghosts?!\""
        },
        {
          "title": "Act 4: The Battle (Pages 31-40)",
          "content": "*Climax: Landauer's Principle & The NULL AXE*\n\n*   **Page 31:** **[Scene: Information Field]**\n    *   *Visual:* Nei stands amidst the chaos.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"This is the Information Field. Images converted to mass.\"\n*   **Page 32:** **[Scene: Explanation]**\n    *   *Visual:* Text overlay: **Landauer's Principle**.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"Information is physics. Deleting a bit generates heat. Malice generates weight.\"\n    *   *Reaction:* Classmate: \"Landauer? Who?\" Nei: \"A physicist.\"\n*   **Page 33:** **[Scene: Ghost Attack]**\n    *   *Visual:* The ghosts (the classmates' own anger) attack them.\n    *   *Action:* A ghost scratches a student. The student bleeds/feels pain.\n    *   *Dialogue:* \"It hurts! Why!?\"\n*   **Page 34:** **[Scene: Chaos]**\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"Ghosts cause Phantom Pain. No physical wound, but the brain feels it.\"\n    *   *Action:* Classmates scream. \"Stop this device!\"\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"I can't. This is *your* malice visualized. I just turned on the light.\"\n*   **Page 35:** **[Scene: Ren's Turn]**\n    *   *Visual:* A ghost lunges at the group.\n    *   *Action:* Ren steps in. \"Ghost Hack time.\"\n*   **Page 36:** **[Scene: NULL AXE]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren pulls a massive, digital axe out of thin air. **NULL AXE**.\n    *   *Action:* SLASH. The ghost is deleted instantly.\n    *   *Reaction:* Classmates: \"An axe?! Dangerous!!\" Nei: \"It's information. Safe.\"\n*   **Page 37:** **[Scene: The Daemon]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto screams. A massive, dark shadow erupts from him.\n    *   *Identifier:* **Daemon: Self-Blame & Debt.**\n    *   *Visuals:* The Daemon is made of credit card bills, insults, and \"Sorry\".\n*   **Page 38:** **[Scene: Ren vs Daemon]**\n    *   *Visual:* The Daemon attacks Ren. Heavy impact.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Daemon (Yuto's voice): \"Too late! Can't be fixed! Unforgivable!\"\n    *   *Action:* Ren blocks, slides back. \"Heavy...\"\n*   **Page 39:** **[Scene: Ren's Logic]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren stands up, dusting off.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Ren: \"Yeah. You can't undo the leak. You can't undo the click.\"\n    *   *Beat:* Ren looks at Yuto.\n*   **Page 40:** **[Scene: The Slash]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren raises the axe.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Ren: \"But... the one who wrote the insults wasn't you. The one who stole the money wasn't you.\"\n    *   *Action:* **\"/dev/null SLASH!!\"**\n    *   *Effect:* Ren cuts the *connection* (the red string of logic) between Yuto and the Malice."
        },
        {
          "title": "Act 5: Resolution (Pages 41-45)",
          "content": "*Falling Action: The Aftermath*\n\n*   **Page 41:** **[Scene: Silence]**\n    *   *Visual:* The Daemon dissolves into particles. The ghosts fade. The room returns to normal (mostly).\n    *   *Action:* Yuto falls to his knees.\n*   **Page 42:** **[Scene: Apology]**\n    *   *Visual:* Yuto looks at the classmates.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Yuto: \"I'm sorry. I was careless. I hurt you.\"\n    *   *Beat:* He owns his mistake, but sheds the guilt of the *crime*.\n    *   *Reaction:* Classmates are stunned. The anger has drained (since Ren cut it). \"Uh... yeah. We said too much too.\"\n*   **Page 43:** **[Scene: The Real Enemy]**\n    *   *Visual:* One classmate tries to blame Yuto again.\n    *   *Action:* Ren interrupts. \"Wrong. The bad guy is the 'Actor' (Hacker).\"\n    *   *Dialogue:* Ren: \"I hate people who make work for me. The guy who made 'Wakuwaku Denki'.\"\n    *   *Visual:* Ren glares at the void (breaking the 4th wall slightly).\n*   **Page 44:** **[Scene: Wrap Up]**\n    *   *Visual:* Classmates swarm Nei. \"What was that device?!\" \"Where do I buy it?!\"\n    *   *Dialogue:* Nei: \"Internet. Site's gone though.\"\n    *   *Action:* Ren yawns. \"Done. Going home to sleep.\" Nei: \"Clean up first.\" Ren: \"Geh.\"\n*   **Page 45:** **[Scene: Epilogue]**\n    *   *Visual:* Ren and Nei on a roof/high place overlooking Tokyo.\n    *   *Dialogue:* Ren: \"Let's go.\" Nei: \"Yeah.\"\n    *   *Text:* **Ghost Hacker.**"
        }
      ]
